WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.990
Let's take a quick look at how to deploy Python
3 applications to Google App Engine. I have

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:09.469
a Python 3 app that runs great on my local
machine, and I want to deploy it to App Engine.

00:00:09.469 --> 00:00:16.199
All my dependencies are listed in my 'requirements.txt'
file. To deploy our code, go to cloud.google.com.

00:00:16.199 --> 00:00:20.529
Sign in to your Google Account if you haven't
done so already, and then go to 'My Console.'

00:00:20.529 --> 00:00:24.150
Make sure you sign up for the free trial if
you haven't done that yet. Now go to "select

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:29.220
a project" and create a project. Give your
project a name, and click "Create." Then,

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:35.010
go to the "Compute Engine" section and make
sure billing is enabled. If you don't have

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:39.180
the Google Cloud SDK installed on your computer,
see the link in the description for how to

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:43.739
install it. Create a file called app.yaml
with the following information. We are using

00:00:43.739 --> 00:00:49.500
Python 3 and gunicorn to run our server. Run
'gcloud init' to login into your Google Account.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:54.609
Now run 'gcloud preview app deploy' to deploy
your application. In a few minutes, your application

00:00:54.609 --> 00:00:59.059
should be deployed. Go to the URL, and you
can see your application running on the cloud!

